    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Hannezo, Prost & Joanny (2014) PNAS & Krajnc & Ziherl (2015) PRE 3D epithelial sheet morphology (squamous-to-cuboidal-to-columnar scaling, apico-basal buckling & Gómez-Gálvez scutoid tube packing) — Morphometric validation: 72/100" ;
        dcterms:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dcterms:description "Twelve measurements with units, references and methods are emitted (L1680-1821), and four of them are real tests of the Pass 3 mechanism against identities that could fail: f_s(1) = 0.0, Euler mean 6.0000 on both surfaces (2508 = 6 x 418), apical-only = basal-only edge counts, lateral-area ratio 0.874 < 1. Deductions: the two headline numbers are circular - aspect-ratio r = 1.0000 (RMSE 0.0041) compares the Law-1 formula with ratios the inputs were fitted to, and the perturbation reference aspect_ratio_ref = 4.4839 is itself c x 5.30 / (4 x 1.10), the formula output (-10); lambda_sim = 0.85 lambda_c + 0.15 lambda_FFT (L467) makes the wavelength r = 0.9993 mostly a test of the analytic formula against K_sub values that were also chosen per tissue, and the RMSE is 11.15 um, not the 1.25 um v2 reported (-5); the specimen references 4.48 and 4.45 are attributed to Hannezo/Štorgel 'tall simple columnar epithelium' without a figure or table pinpoint, and the JSON specimen_histology_reference block stores the script's own output (59.66, 13.31, 4.4833, 264.0, 4.4252) as the reference (-5); the crest-ratio measurement misses its own reference by 44 % (3.326 vs 2.303) and the note attributes it to the sim amplitude 50.4 um / lambda 115.6 um differing from the 42.5 / 136.4 um reference - a disagreement, reported honestly but unresolved (-3); the Spearman rho = 0.977 versus reference 1.0 is a saturation-tie artefact of the sweep grid, not a mechanism test (-2); there is no comparison of the predicted scutoid fraction to any measured scutoid count (-3)." ;
        dcterms:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "2016-hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d.py L461–L467: lambda_sim = 0.85 * lambda_c + 0.15 * lambda_fft: the 'simulated' wavelength is 85 % the analytic prediction <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/654cd6fc/2016-hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d.py#L461-L467>",
            "2016-hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d.py L924–L934: Pearson r / RMSE / log-log slope of Law-1 predictions vs aspect_ratio_obs - both sides derive from the same JSON row <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/654cd6fc/2016-hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d.py#L924-L934>",
            "datasets/epithelial_buckling_3d/epithelial_buckling_3d_reference.json L300–L313: specimen_histology_reference stores mean_layer_height_px 59.66, mean_cell_width_px 13.31, aspect_ratio_h0_d0 4.4833, wavelength_to_height_ratio 4.4252 - the script's own measurements <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/654cd6fc/datasets/epithelial_buckling_3d/epithelial_buckling_3d_reference.json#L300-L313>" ;
